:Namespace Tester
    ⍝ Unit testing framework.
    ⍝
    ⍝ A suite is a namespace. A test is a dfn whose name starts with test_.
    ⍝ The runner calls every test as:  fixture test case
    ⍝   fixture  result of the suite's optional Setup function, run once per
    ⍝            suite; ⍬ when the suite has no Setup
    ⍝   case     the case data for a parameterised test; ⍬ otherwise
    ⍝
    ⍝ Optional suite members:
    ⍝   Setup              monadic function, called with ⍬
    ⍝   <test>_cases       vector of (label data) pairs; the test runs once
    ⍝                      per pair with data as ⍵
    ⍝   Slow               vector of test names skipped unless slow is set
    ⍝
    ⍝ Tests run in alphabetical order of name and must not depend on each
    ⍝ other. The fixture is shared by every test in the suite, so tests must
    ⍝ treat it as read-only.

    ⎕IO ⎕ML←1

    FAIL_EN←777
    PREFIX←'test_'

    ⍝ Assertions
    ⍝ Each assertion returns 1 on success, so a dfn test can end with one.
    ⍝ On failure it signals FAIL_EN, which the runner reports as FAIL rather
    ⍝ than ERROR.

    Fail←{
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ failure message
        ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' FAIL_EN)('Message'(,⍕⍵))
    }

    Eq←{
        ⍝ ⍺ ←→ expected value
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ actual value
        ⍺≡⍵:1
        Fail'expected ',(Show ⍺),' but got ',Show ⍵
    }

    Ok←{
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ value that must be exactly 1
        1≡⍵:1
        Fail'expected 1 but got ',Show ⍵
    }

    Raises←{
        ⍝ (fn Raises en) arg
        ⍝ ⍺⍺ ←→ function under test
        ⍝ ⍵⍵ ←→ expected error number
        ⍝ ⍵  ←→ argument passed to ⍺⍺
        fn←⍺⍺
        got←{0::⎕DMX.EN ⋄ 0⊣fn ⍵}⍵
        got≡⍵⍵:1
        got≡0:Fail'expected error ',(⍕⍵⍵),' but no error was signalled'
        Fail'expected error ',(⍕⍵⍵),' but got error ',⍕got
    }

    ⍝ Array notation serialiser. Interactive sessions provide it as
    ⍝ ⎕SE.Dyalog.Array; dyalogscript starts with an empty ⎕SE, so it is
    ⍝ loaded from the installation instead.
    LoadArrayNotation←{
        0::⎕FIX'file://',(2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'DYALOG'),'/StartupSession/Dyalog/Array.apln'
        ⎕SE.Dyalog.Array
    }
    ArrayNotation←LoadArrayNotation ⍬

    Show←{
        ⍝ Single-line array notation, so shape and type differences are
        ⍝ visible: (1⋄) vs 1, ⍬ vs '', '1' vs 1.
        ⍝ The serialiser pads brackets with diamonds ([⋄1 2⋄3 4⋄]); those are
        ⍝ removed outside string literals. Parentheses keep theirs, because
        ⍝ (1⋄) is how a one-item vector is written.
        s←⊃1 ArrayNotation.Serialise ⍵
        '''[^'']*''' '\[⋄' '⋄\]'⎕R(,¨'&[]')⊢s
    }

    ⍝ Runner

    Run←{
        ⍝ ⍺ ←→ optional namespace: filter (text, default '') and slow (0/1, default 0)
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ suite reference, or vector of suite references
        ⍝ ← ←→ results matrix, one row per test case:
        ⍝      suite name, test name, status, message
        ⍝      status is one of 'PASS' 'FAIL' 'ERROR' 'SKIP'
        ⍺←()
        (filter slow)←⍺ ⎕VGET('filter' '')('slow' 0)
        results←⊃⍪/(⊂0 4⍴⊂''),(⊂filter slow)RunSuite¨,⍵
        _←Report results
        results
    }

    ∇ results←options RunSuite suite;filter;slow;names;fixture;setupError;name;cases;case;label;full;slowNames;sname
      (filter slow)←options
      sname←SuiteName suite
      results←0 4⍴⊂''
      names←{⍵/⍨(⊂PREFIX)≡¨(≢PREFIX)↑¨⍵}suite.⎕NL ¯3
      names←names/⍨(⊂filter)Matches¨(⊂sname),¨'.',¨DisplayName¨names
      →(0=≢names)⍴0
      slowNames←{2=⍵.⎕NC'Slow':,⊆⍵.Slow ⋄ ⍬}suite

      fixture←⍬ ⋄ setupError←''
      :If 3=suite.⎕NC'Setup'
          :Trap 0
              fixture←suite.Setup ⍬
          :Else
              setupError←'Setup failed: ',ErrorText ⍬
          :EndTrap
      :EndIf

      :For name :In names
          cases←,⊂''⍬
          :If 2=suite.⎕NC name,'_cases'
              cases←suite⍎name,'_cases'
          :EndIf
          :For (label case) :In cases
              full←(DisplayName name),(0≠≢label)/' [',label,']'
              :If (~slow)∧(⊂name)∊slowNames
                  results⍪←sname full'SKIP' ''
              :ElseIf 0≠≢setupError
                  results⍪←sname full'ERROR'setupError
              :Else
                  results⍪←sname full,fixture RunOne suite name case
              :EndIf
          :EndFor
      :EndFor
    ∇

    ∇ result←fixture RunOne(suite name case);test
      ⍝ ← ←→ status message
      test←suite⍎name
      :Trap 0
          {}fixture test case
          result←'PASS' ''
      :Else
          :If FAIL_EN=⎕DMX.EN
              result←'FAIL'⎕DMX.Message
          :Else
              result←'ERROR'(ErrorText ⍬)
          :EndIf
      :EndTrap
    ∇

    ErrorText←{
        ⍝ Error name, message and offending line from the current ⎕DMX.
        dm←⎕DMX.DM ⋄ msg←⎕DMX.Message
        line←{(∨\⍵≠' ')/⍵}{⍵/⍨~⌽∧\⌽⍵=' '}2⊃dm,⊂''
        (⊃dm),((0≠≢msg)/': ',msg),(0≠≢line)/' in: ',line
    }

    DisplayName←{
        ⍝ test_places_pawns ←→ 'places pawns'
        ' '@(=∘'_')(≢PREFIX)↓⍵
    }

    Matches←{
        ⍝ Case-insensitive substring match; an empty filter matches everything.
        0=≢⍺:1
        ∨/(⎕C ⍺)⍷⎕C ⍵
    }

    ⍝ Reporting

    ∇ {r}←Report results;row;status;counts;words
      ⍝ Prints one line per test, failure details, and a summary.
      r←⍬
      :For row :In ↓results
          status←3⊃row
          ⍞←status,((6-≢status)⍴' '),(1⊃row),' ',(2⊃row),⎕UCS 10
          :If (⊂status)∊'FAIL' 'ERROR'
              ⍞←'      ',(4⊃row),⎕UCS 10
          :EndIf
      :EndFor
      counts←+/'PASS' 'FAIL' 'ERROR' 'SKIP'∘.≡results[;3]
      words←'passed' 'failed' 'errored' 'skipped'
      ⍞←(⎕UCS 10),(¯2↓∊(⍕¨counts),¨' ',¨words,¨⊂', '),⎕UCS 10
    ∇

    SuiteName←{
        ⍝ #.BoardTests ←→ 'BoardTests'
        ⊃⌽'.'(≠⊆⊢)⍕⍵
    }

    Failed←{
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ results matrix from Run
        ⍝ ← ←→ 1 if any test failed or errored
        ∨/(⍵[;3])∊'FAIL' 'ERROR'
    }

:EndNamespace
